# Wisp Technologies Portfolio - Complete Development Guide

## 🏗️ **Project Architecture**
- **Framework**: Next.js 15 with App Router
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS with CSS variables for theming
- **UI Components**: shadcn/ui components with custom styling
- **Animations**: GSAP for text reveals and transitions
- **Theme System**: next-themes for light/dark mode switching

## 📁 **Key Files & Directories**
- [src/app/layout.tsx](mdc:src/app/layout.tsx) - Root layout with theme provider
- [src/app/providers.tsx](mdc:src/app/providers.tsx) - App providers and transition router
- [src/app/globals.css](mdc:src/app/globals.css) - Global styles and CSS variables
- [src/components/ui/](mdc:src/components/ui/) - shadcn/ui components
- [src/hooks/useTextReveal.ts](mdc:src/hooks/useTextReveal.ts) - GSAP animation hooks
- [DESIGN_SYSTEM.md](mdc:DESIGN_SYSTEM.md) - Complete design system documentation

## 🎨 **Design System**
- **Minimal & Clean**: No borders, lots of whitespace, crisp typography
- **Modern & Futuristic**: Clean lines, subtle gradients, contemporary feel
- **Professional**: No emojis, text-only approach
- **Wisp Theme**: Light guiding through darkness, illuminating technology

### **Color System**
Use CSS variables from [src/app/globals.css](mdc:src/app/globals.css):
- `--background` and `--foreground` for primary colors
- Opacity variations: `/10`, `/20`, `/60`, `/70`, `/90`
- Gradients: `bg-gradient-to-br from-background via-background to-muted/20`

### **Typography**
- **Headings**: Large, thin fonts with tight tracking
- **Body**: Clean, readable text with proper line height
- **Fonts**: Inter/SF Pro Display for headings, JetBrains Mono for technical text
- **Hierarchy**: Clear visual hierarchy with size and weight variations

### **Spacing & Layout**
- **Generous whitespace**: Large margins and padding
- **Grid layouts**: Clean grid systems with proper gaps
- **Consistent spacing**: 6, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24px scale
- **No borders**: Avoid border classes, use spacing instead

## 🎭 **Animation Guidelines**
- **GSAP Text Reveal**: Staggered text animations with clipPath masks
- **Smooth transitions**: 300ms duration, power2 easing
- **Hover effects**: Subtle scale (1.05x) and opacity changes
- **Loading states**: Ultra-slow, meditative animations

### **Animation Hooks**
Use the established animation hooks from [src/hooks/useTextReveal.ts](mdc:src/hooks/useTextReveal.ts):
```typescript
const titleRef = useTextReveal({ delay: 0, duration: 0.8, from: "bottom" });
const contentRefs = useStaggeredTextReveal<HTMLDivElement>(3, {
  delay: 0.8,
  stagger: 0.3,
  from: "bottom",
});
```

## 🧩 **Component Development**

### **shadcn/ui Integration**
- Always use shadcn/ui components as base: [src/components/ui/](mdc:src/components/ui/)
- Install new components with: `npx shadcn@latest add [component-name]`
- Customize using CSS variables and Tailwind classes
- Maintain consistent theming across all components

### **Theme Integration**
- Use CSS variables for all colors: `text-foreground`, `bg-background`
- Apply opacity variations: `text-foreground/60`, `bg-foreground/10`
- Test both light and dark themes
- Ensure proper contrast ratios

### **Data-Driven Components**
- Use arrays for repetitive content (like team members)
- Create reusable component patterns
- Maintain consistent data structures
- Use TypeScript interfaces for type safety

## 🌙 **Theme System**
- Theme provider in [src/app/layout.tsx](mdc:src/app/layout.tsx)
- Theme toggle component: [src/components/theme-toggle.tsx](mdc:src/components/theme-toggle.tsx)
- CSS variables defined in [src/app/globals.css](mdc:src/app/globals.css)
- Supports light/dark modes with system preference detection

### **Theme-Aware Components**
When creating new components:
1. Use CSS variables instead of hardcoded colors
2. Test in both light and dark modes
3. Apply consistent opacity variations
4. Ensure proper contrast and readability

## 📱 **Responsive Design**
- Mobile-first approach
- Clean mobile layouts
- Proper breakpoint usage: sm, md, lg, xl
- Typography scaling for different screen sizes
- Grid adaptations: Single column on mobile

